\r\nThe project syncs and runs fine. There is a warning that reads \"API 'variant.getJavaCompile()' is obsolete and has been replaced with 'variant.getJavaCompileProvider()'\"\r\n\r\nThe obsolete method call can be found in ExoPlayer\\javadoc_library.gradle:24\r\n\r\n### Reproduction steps\r\n1. Upgrade gradle tools to 3.3.0\r\n2. Add 'android.debug.obsoleteApi=true' to gradle.properties file which will log error with a more details\r\n3. Sync project again\r\n\r\n### Link to test content\r\nhttps://stackoverflow.com/questions/52470044/warning-api-variant-getjavacompile-is-obsolete-and-has-been-replaced-with\r\n\r\n### Version of ExoPlayer being used\r\nbranch dev-v2\r\n\r\n### Device(s) and version(s) of Android being used\r\ncom.android.tools.build:gradle:3.3.0\r\nThe project syncs and runs fine. It is a warning, not an error. But here is what I am using to run the project:\r\nMotorola Moto Z Play Droid - Motorola XT1635-01(Android 8.0.0, API 26)\r\n\r\n\r\n### A full bug report captured from the device\r\nThis is the full warning after the debug line is added to the gradle.properties file.\r\n\r\nWARNING: API 'variant.getJavaCompile()' is obsolete and has been replaced with 'variant.getJavaCompileProvider()'.\r\nIt will be removed at the end of 2019.\r\nFor more information, see https://d.android.com/r/tools/task-configuration-avoidance.\r\nREASON: Called from: ExoPlayer\\javadoc_library.gradle:24\r\nWARNING: Debugging obsolete API calls can take time during configuration. It's recommended to not keep it on at all times.\r\nAffected Modules: extension-cast\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"tonihei","id":26897506,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2ODk3NTA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26897506?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonihei","html_url":"https://github.com/tonihei","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonihei/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tonihei/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"h